Andrew,

Everything is attached.  I apologize for not labeling the models in the order that they were run, but you should be able to see what's what from the R code.

Good call on losing simulations.  That makes a lot of sense given that we see things maxing out at 10K effective samples.  With 4 chains at 10K iterations a piece and 5K warmup runs per chain, we'd expect to get 20K simulations under completely independent sampling. Obviously we don't usually expect perfectly independent draws, but I think you can see where I'm going here.  Outside of getting the maximum 20K, getting something like an even 10K is a little suspicious.

I just looked at output produced via print and I'm getting effective sample sizes of 20K in some places which would explain the difference I saw between print and monitor.  Do you think the monitor issue alone is enough to explain the apparent disparities between Stan and JAGS?  I was seeing similar results when using the print command, though I don't think the sample size calculations were perfectly comparable in that context.

Adam

