> >         I get another parser error:
> >
> >              mismatched dimensions on left- and right-hand side of assignment; left dims=1; right dims=0
> >
> >         I'm aware that I can loop over the indices of a to assign each element of b, but I'm of the (possibly mistaken?)
> >         impression from my R experiences that such loops are inefficient relative to vectorized approaches. This,
> >         however, presumes that a vectorized approach exists... does it?
> >
> >
> >     The issue is that the return of normal_log(a, 0, 1) is going to be real. A single value. In this case, the return of:
> >     normal_log(a,0,1)
> >
> >     is equivalent to:
> >     normal_log(a[1],0,1) + normal_log(a[2],0,1)
> >
> >     Hopefully that clears up the confusion.
> >
> >
> >     What are you trying to do? If you want to store the unnormalized log of the normal pdf evaluated for each element of
> >     a, you could loop, but I'm not sure if that's what you actually want to do. From the modeling language, I don't
> >     think there is a way to ask for the normalized log pdf value for any of our distributions, so for this case, it will
> >     return -a[1]^2/2 - a[2]^2/2.
